      "writtenOn": "2023-06-21T20:14:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s more precise if you parse the task ID by `HANDLER EXCEPTION` or \"PROCESS EXCEPTION\".\n\nFor example, if a divide-by-zero crash happens in an interrupt handler, then the regs[0] is still not the task ID but a handler\u0027s ID. You might want to add regs[\"handler\"] as a new dict entry.\n\nR5 provides additional context of the task ID only if it\u0027s a stack-overflow crash.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "e2f992e78b7cf9d7bfcb25ed81337f1c00491d0e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
